    {
      "code": "photo_scaled_architecture",
      "detail": "Vault proportions, 13 repeated arches, 0.34 m niche depth relative to the plaster skin, 0.14 m shell thickness, apron projection and coffer depth are photo-scaled estimates, including the owner-supplied 10429.jpg. The white curved skin has closed front/back/end/underside faces and overlays the brown wall. Signage repeats name/empty/route/empty. Three square information pylons are retained. Station Base dimensions and connection points are unchanged; no survey or scan is claimed."
    },
    {
      "code": "material_adaptation",
      "detail": "Procedural grain and plaster, world-space texture coordinates, native TextMesh font generation and live SubViewport mirror imagery require adaptation/baking for future export. Native meshes/MultiMeshes, textures and font outlines remain accessible."
    },
    {
      "code": "vestibule_continuations",
      "detail": "Visible stairs and upper gate halls are represented; unphotographed side corridors continue into dim space. No surrounding city or railway platform is invented."
    },
